messages:
zoe_sales: Leo from NovaHealth just called 520 - their POC demo stalled. Mobile webview throws JSON.parse errors and stream drops after ~40s.
max_se: Any logs or a network snippet? Is desktop affected?
leo_customer: Only our Android/iOS webview. Desktop Chrome is fine. Client error: "Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected end of JSON input at parseSse (app.bundle.js:220)". Network shows SSE data lines that sometimes cut mid-object. Sample copied from capture:

event: message
data: {\"seq\":3,\"text\":\"Hello\"}

event: message
data: {\"seq\":4,\"text\":\"This is a very lo

\"

Client tries JSON.parse on second payload and fails.
jana_oncall: Infra: I see a short spike of 429s for their org and a handful of proxy resets at the same time. Edge logs: "recv() failed (104: Connection reset by peer)" and upstream: "client prematurely closed connection". Proxy buffering warnings also present. Could be fragmentation + retry overlap.
max_se: Two likely issues: (1) client assumes each data: block is a complete JSON object and parses immediately, (2) proxy/network truncation or early close fragments payloads.
zoe_sales: Customer asked for a fast mitigation before tomorrow's exec demo. Can we push something now?
jana_oncall: Short-term infra fixes we can do immediately: lower gateway retry concurrency for their API key (to avoid retry storms), disable proxy_buffering for streaming routes on canary, and emit SSE heartbeat comments (":\n") every 12s from canary to keep connections alive. I'll apply the throttle now.
max_se: On the client side, recommend an accumulator approach in the webview so it tolerates split JSON across multiple data: events. Here's a tiny non-invasive snippet they can inject without rebuilding their wrapper:
```js
let acc = '';
function onSseData(dataLine) {
  acc += dataLine;
  try {
    const msg = JSON.parse(acc);
    handleMessage(msg);
    acc = '';
  } catch (e) {
    // incomplete - wait for next chunk
    if (acc.length > 128*1024) { acc = ''; console.warn('dropping oversized partial'); }
  }
}
```
Add a short flush timeout (5s) to avoid stuck buffers.
ci-bot: canary v2.26.0 deployed to eu-west-1 at 2130003200
leo_customer: We'll try injecting the shim and confirm. Please apply the infra changes now.
jana_oncall: Actions: (1) throttle retries for org (applied) (2) disable proxy_buffering on canary for SSE routes (applied) (3) enable 12s heartbeat comments from canary (in progress) (4) add metric to track partial-parse rate (queued). I'll follow up in #eng-runtime if rollouts change.
zoe_sales: Thanks team. Leo, ping us after you test the shim and infra tweaks. Marking this as high-touch POC support until the exec demo completes. :thumbsup:
leo_customer: Injecting shim now, will test in ~20m and update here. Thanks for the fast help.
